---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Free Forex Signal Robots | BlueFx Markets" description="Free sample forex signal robots from BlueFx Markets. Alerts only, no live orders." page="robots">
<main id="content">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Tools / Free Forex Signal Robots</p>
      <h1>Free Forex signal robots</h1>
      <p class="lede">Three robots you can switch on in this browser. They describe a sample alert. They do not attach to MT5 and they do not move a NAD balance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="bot-grid" id="robot-grid">
        <article class="bot">
          <header><h3>Kunene Trend</h3><span class="pill">NAD crosses</span></header>
          <p>Watches USD/NAD, EUR/NAD and GBP/NAD through the London morning, which is late morning in Windhoek. A sample alert names a direction and a distance. It is not an order.</p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Symbols</dt><dd>USD/NAD, EUR/NAD</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Style</dt><dd>Trend</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Session</dt><dd>08:00–12:00 CAT</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd>Free</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" data-robot="Kunene Trend">Enable on demo</button>
        </article>
        <article class="bot">
          <header><h3>Etosha Gold</h3><span class="pill hot">Metals</span></header>
          <p>Posts a sample note when gold moves against the Namibian Dollar. Useful next to the gold seminar. The robot does not sell or buy XAU/NAD for you.</p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Symbols</dt><dd>XAU/NAD, XAU/USD</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Style</dt><dd>Swing</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Session</dt><dd>London and New York</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd>Free</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" data-robot="Etosha Gold">Enable on demo</button>
        </article>
        <article class="bot">
          <header><h3>Atlantic Range</h3><span class="pill">Majors</span></header>
          <p>Looks for a quiet range on EUR/USD and GBP/USD, then writes a sample alert in NAD terms so the distance is easy to read from Windhoek.</p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Symbols</dt><dd>EUR/USD, GBP/USD</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Style</dt><dd>Range</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Session</dt><dd>14:00–18:00 CAT</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Cost</dt><dd>Free</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" data-robot="Atlantic Range">Enable on demo</button>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="note" id="robot-note">Signals can be wrong. Enabling a robot here only changes this page. Compare them with the free signal bots if you want the running sample feed.</p>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:16px">
        <a class="btn btn-line" href="/signals">Free signal bots</a>
        <a class="btn btn-line" href="/seminars">Free seminars</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById("robot-grid").addEventListener("click", (event) => {
      const button = event.target.closest("[data-robot]");
      if (!button) return;
      const on = button.dataset.on === "1";
      button.dataset.on = on ? "0" : "1";
      button.textContent = on ? "Enable on demo" : "Enabled on this demo";
      document.getElementById("robot-note").textContent = on
        ? "Signals can be wrong. Enabling a robot here only changes this page."
        : button.dataset.robot + " is marked on in this browser. No alert was sent and no NAD balance changed.";
    });
  </script>
</main>
</Base>
